   "relevant": true,
   "speaker": "Michele Bullock",
   "role": "Governor",
   "points": [
    "Inflation is expected to run above the August forecasts, as higher oil prices, elevated short-term expectations and domestic capacity pressures add to price growth.",
    "The labour market looks somewhat tighter than judged earlier, and further subdued demand growth is needed to bring inflation down sustainably.",
    "The Monetary Policy Board meets next week to judge whether the tightening so far will return inflation to target in a reasonable time."
   ],
   "stance": "hawkish",
   "score": 1,
   "reason": "Worse inflation outlook, tighter labour market, tightening may not suffice"
  }
